                <pb facs="0298" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg202"/>

                <head>A.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jenkins to
                        Mr. Shepard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-11-01"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 1,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to hand you the original order which
                    was sent to my agent at Chung Ching, in Chinese, with a copy of it in English.
                    It is from Lee, the magistrate of Chung Ching. It explains itself. I have to
                    request that you will forward a copy of it to his excellency the minister at
                    Peking, and have most respectfully to ask that steps be taken as early as
                    possible to prevent further heavy loss. I shall forward, as soon as received,
                    particulars of a claim for loss of market, interest, &amp;c.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>M. ANDREW JENKINS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
